+## Results-hang fixes (2026-11-14, exvs2-lobbies `analysis/results-hang-fixes.md` section 4) — fake cabinets only
+All off by default except the log line. Tests: `Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/HangFixTests.cs`,
+exvs2-lobbies `server-sketch/loadtest/hangfix_e2e.py`.
+* `OnlineMatching.HumansTeamVsCpu` (false): a short-handed room with exactly two humans (two solos, or a 2-human team
+  waiting alone) makes them **teammates** (group 0) against two CPU stand-ins (group 1, `PCB00000NPC` / "N", each on
+  one human's own 2nd IssueNodeId id, listed after the humans). Instead of the usual 1v1 where each human has a CPU
+  partner. Needs `AllowPartialRooms`; waits `FillAfterSeconds` for a real 2v2 first. 3-human short rooms, full rooms and
+  cabinets that brought their own CPU partner are unchanged. If a stand-in id would collide with a human node, the
+  normal 1v1 forms. **Untested with the game:** whether it accepts a side with no human is unknown.
+* `PostMatchStubs` (false): minimal answers instead of `ErrServer "Unhandled case"` for SaveVsmToResult (205),
+  SaveFailedBattleLogOn (225), RegisterOption (306): Success, empty body; SaveMedal (211): ACID_SUCCESS + pilot id,
+  0 medals (ACID_NO_USE if the card is unknown); LoadReplayCard (406): ACID_NO_USE; PreSaveReplay (407): status 2
+  (reject) + `http://dummy`, so the LM skips its replay upload. Nothing is stored; log lines start with `STUB`.
+* `LogNetworkReport` (true): one `NETREPORT` line per SaveVsmOnResult: input / start delay frames, delay source, pause
+  count/frames, and per cabinet `serial@loc:rtt,max,loss`. No card data.
+
 ## Known gaps / risks
 * CheckMatching / CancelMatching are not authenticated: anyone who knows a node id can cancel that entry.
 * Malformed protobuf bodies on `/match` get HTTP 500 from the model binder (the real cabinet never sends them).
