@@ -97,6 +98,13 @@ Card data (ChipId / AccessCode / BootToken) and `pcb_serial` are never logged. O
 * `drop nodes=[..] reason=...` (replaced by re-entry / same cabinet entered again / matching timeout /
   cancelled by node N / stopped polling (stale)).
 * `VerboseLog: true` adds `check node=N -> <code> room=R` per poll.
+* `LogPostMatchTraffic` (true, logging only): for 30 min after a cabinet's room was made, every request it makes to
+  this matchmaker gets an `MMS-POST <method> node=N [apply=A] src=<ip> -> <code> [room=R] (<ms>ms) room=R +Ts by=node|ip`
+  line (keep-polling CheckMatching at most every 15 s per node), and STUN binding requests from its IP a
+  `STUN-POST from=<ip:port> change=.. room=R +Ts by=ip` line (at most every 10 s per sender). `+Ts` = seconds since the
+  room was made, so traffic during or after the battle shows directly. Unknown MMS methods always give
+  `MMS-UNHANDLED method=typeN ...` (warning). No pcb serial, am id or card data in these lines. The matchmaker never
+  calls a cabinet, an LM or another card server itself; these lines show what the cabinets call.
 Request source is the TCP peer (`RemoteIpAddress`, IPv4-mapped shown as IPv4); proxy headers are not trusted.
 
 ## One server for LM and non-LM players (2026-11-13, exvs2-lobbies `analysis/lm-and-online.md`)
