Subject: [PATCH 25/26] Add cross-server online tag with shared partner codes
 and settings sync

Players on different card servers can form an online-tag team by exchanging
an 8-character partner code on the WebUI Teams tab. Each card keeps a
globally unique wire pilot / am id (ServerId * 1_000_000 + local id). The
shared matchmaker /tag store holds the invite, and world 5 pairs searchers
who share that code. Team name, BGM, effect, background, emblem and name
color are pushed to /tag on save and pulled on LoadCard and the Teams tab
(last write wins). Same-server User ID + Invitation Code is unchanged.
Realms, NoCpuPartner, 1on1 and rolling fill are unchanged. No game-exe
patch. 169 unit tests; two-card-server e2e covers colliding local ids,
settings sync and world-5 pairing.

