From b368843e325e0442b605002e7e821f9f19f60fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ServerOmega <69215510+ServerOmega@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:00:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] Default OnlineTag.TagStatus to 1 so the in-game list is
 selectable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With TagStatus 0, LoadCard sent tag_teams=1 but both cabinets showed an
empty, greyed-out オンラインタッグ panel on TEAM SELECT (live 2026-11-15).
The documented next value is 1; that is now the default and stays
configurable. Confirmed in the real game at 5:57 AM Pacific Time: both
cabs listed the shared team, searched world 5, and the VPS paired them.

Co-authored-by: Grok Bot <grok-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md                           |  4 ++--
 Server-Infinite/Configurations/server.json      |  2 +-
 .../Models/Config/OnlineTagConfigurations.cs    |  8 +++++---
 Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/OnlineTagConfigTests.cs | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Tests/Matchmaking.Tests/OnlineTagConfigTests.cs

diff --git a/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md b/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
index 20678b7..a045fd7 100644
--- a/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
+++ b/ONLINE_MATCHMAKING.md
@@ -138,7 +138,7 @@ Class 14), which matches like any other team.
 | Piece | What this patch does |
 |---|---|
 | Invite (WebUI **Teams** tab, re-enabled) | Player A enters partner B's **User ID** + B's **Invitation Code** → a tag team A+B on the server. The server now checks the code itself (upstream trusted the WebUI), refuses a team with yourself / a duplicate / more than 20 per card, and (default) B gets a new code after it was used (`OneTimeInviteCode`). A new team no longer crashes the tab (BGM 0). |
